<DocsLayout title="Advanced Strands Agents guide | Agent-Gantry" description="Approval through Strands interrupts, per-turn selection, run context and error modes for the Agent-Gantry Strands Agents integration.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Advanced framework guide</p>
  <h1>Advanced Strands Agents</h1>
  <p class="lead">Interrupt-based approval, how per-turn selection works, and run context.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/Agent-Gantry/docs/frameworks/strands/">← Basic Strands usage</a></p>

  <h2>Approval through interrupts</h2>
  <p>A confirmation-gated call (<code>requires_confirmation=True</code> or a <code>SecurityPolicy(require_confirmation=[...])</code> pattern) raises a Strands interrupt from inside the tool, named <code>"gantry-approval"</code> with a reason holding the tool, its arguments and description. The run stops with <code>stop_reason == "interrupt"</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`result = await agent.invoke_async("Refund order 4471")
if result.stop_reason == "interrupt":
    [interrupt] = result.interrupts
    answer = "yes" if ask_a_human(interrupt.reason) else "no"
    result = await agent.invoke_async(
        [{"interruptResponse": {"interruptId": interrupt.id, "response": answer}}]
    )`} />
  <p>The tool re-runs on resume and the interrupt returns the response: <code>"yes"</code>, <code>"y"</code>, <code>"approve"</code>, <code>"approved"</code>, <code>True</code> or <code>&#123;"approved": True&#125;</code> runs the call once through <code>gantry.execute</code> with only the confirmation gate cleared; anything else rejects it and the model is told. A tool called directly, outside an agent, reports that it needs approval.</p>

  <h2>Per-turn selection</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mechanism:</strong> <code>tool_hook()</code> handles <code>BeforeModelCallEvent</code> and swaps the agent's tool registry before Strands reads it, so the selection applies to the call about to happen.</li>
    <li><strong>Query:</strong> the latest user message.</li>
    <li><strong>Failure:</strong> the registry is stateful, so if retrieval fails the previous turn's tools stay registered and a warning is logged.</li>
    <li>Tools registered by the hook use the adapter's error mode and formatter, and interrupt for approval like static ones.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Run context and tracing</h2>
  <p><code>current_tool_context()</code> returns Strands' <code>ToolContext</code>: <code>.invocation_state</code> (the keyword arguments passed to <code>agent(...)</code>), <code>.agent</code> and <code>.tool_use</code>. <code>current_tool_invocation()</code> carries it too, with <code>deps</code> set to <code>invocation_state</code> and <code>tool_call_id</code> to the <code>toolUseId</code>. Strands traces with OpenTelemetry, so its span becomes the Gantry <code>ToolCall</code>'s trace.</p>
</DocsLayout>
